flowchart TB
  accTitle: How the visual check and the screenshot bot render the images in groups
  accDescr: Each language renders in three groups at once, each group on a runner of its own from a fresh demo. The cards and the first games make group 1, more games with the players group 2, the corrections of a dart, the formats, the big tournaments, the calendar and the dartboard without Autodarts group 3. Then one job per language puts the images of its three groups together and compares them with the committed images. The visual check writes the comparison into one comment on the pull request; the screenshot bot updates its pull request with every language that rendered.

  START["A pull request or a push to main<br/>changes the cards or the screenshot tool"] --> G1 & G2 & G3
  G1["Group 1, a fresh demo:<br/>the cards, the live card,<br/>the first games, about 8 min"]
  G2["Group 2, a fresh demo:<br/>more games, a tournament,<br/>then the players, about 11 min"]
  G3["Group 3, a fresh demo:<br/>the corrections, the formats,<br/>the big tournaments up to their pictures,<br/>the calendar, the manual board, about 10 min"]
  G1 & G2 & G3 --> COLLECT["One job per language puts<br/>its groups together and compares<br/>them with the committed images"]
  COLLECT --> COMMENT["Visual check: one comment<br/>on the pull request"]
  COLLECT --> BOT["Screenshot bot: its pull request<br/>with every language that rendered"]

  classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
  classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
  class G1,G2,G3,COLLECT bot
  class COMMENT,BOT done
